# Substack Cover Art

Generate cover images when the user asks for a Substack (or external-platform) cover while drafting a hidden post.

## File location

```
assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/cover.png
```

- `{media}` = post `media_type` (e.g. `substack`, `youtube`, `wechat`); main-site posts use `site`
- `{YYYY-MM-DD}` = post `date` in front matter
- Set in post front matter: `substack_cover: /assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/cover.png`

Example: `assets/img/blog/substack-2026-07-03/cover.png`

## Visual style (user reference aesthetic)

- **16:9 wide** landscape, suitable for Substack hero/cover
- **High-contrast black & white** conceptual editorial illustration — ink-on-paper feel
- **Mood:** intellectual, calm, slightly surreal; professional thinking / strategy / urban-tech writing
- **Composition varies by article** — derive from the post thesis when generating; do not reuse a fixed template
- **No mandatory tropes** — do not default to recurring motifs (e.g. tiny figure vs. data wave) unless the user asks
- **No text, logos, or watermarks** in the image

## Prompting

- Describe **style only** in the rule; at generation time, derive abstract visual direction from the article thesis (not the title alone)
- Style keywords: high-contrast monochrome, conceptual editorial illustration, ink/graphite texture, clean negative space, surreal but restrained, intellectual mood
- Avoid literal UI mockups, readable text, logos, and stock-photo clichés
- Keep monochrome; avoid color unless the user explicitly asks

## Workflow

1. Read post `date`, `media_type`, and thesis from front matter / draft
2. Generate with `GenerateImage`; pass user reference covers if available via `reference_image_paths`
3. Save to `assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/cover.png`
4. Add or update `substack_cover` in the post front matter

## Do not

- Save covers under `assets/img/substack/` (deprecated)
- Use slug-only filenames without `{media}-{date}` folder
- Reuse the same composition for every article
